{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775232196,"nonce":"C1T2ZaRexMoAzObjPEkgGGfPmtU=","title":"Codex agent fails inside Docker because ~/.codex/config.toml is only generated when OVERFLOW_API_KEY is set, but non-overflow Codex sessions don't have overflow env vars.","message":"docker-entrypoint.sh generates ~/.codex/config.toml only when OVERFLOW_API_KEY is set. But when agent.kind is codex (not overflow mode), OVERFLOW_API_KEY isn't passed to the container. The Codex CLI then fails with \"Missing required environment variable(s): LLM_API_KEY, LLM_MODEL\".\n\nEvidence: session ce5dcc9a8193 raw-output.log shows repeated auth errors.\n\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_codex_agent_gets_overflow_env_vars\n  Assert: when agent.kind is codex, docker command includes OVERFLOW_API_KEY even without overflow flag\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_non_codex_agent_no_extra_env\n  Assert: when agent.kind is claude-code, no extra overflow env vars added\n\n- host/docker_cmd.py (modify — pass OVERFLOW_* env vars when agent kind is codex)\n- host/launch.py (modify — pass agent_kind to run_container so docker_cmd can check it)\n\n1. In host/launch.py, detect agent kind from config and pass it to run_container\n2. In host/docker_cmd.py build_docker_cmd(), when the agent kind is \"codex\", always inject OVERFLOW_API_KEY, OVERFLOW_BASE_URL, OVERFLOW_MODEL from os.environ (same as passthrough vars) so docker-entrypoint.sh can generate the config.toml\n3. Alternative: generate config.toml from any available key — check OPENAI_API_KEY, OVERFLOW_API_KEY, or a new CODEX_API_KEY\n\nSee _PASSTHROUGH_ENV_VARS in host/docker_cmd.py for env var forwarding.\n\nREQ: REQ-033","files":null}]}